{
  "_what_this_is": [
    "The project's capacity record: what its quota windows held, as they were last",
    "observed, and what is held back. tools/capacity_record.py is the ONE writer —",
    "a document it did not write is read as the older 2.5.0 shape and reported as",
    "such, never repaired on read.",
    "The timestamps below are placeholders in the year 2000, so this example reads",
    "STALE by construction and can never look fresh. Freshness is computed at READ",
    "time against the reading's own source horizon (freshness_horizon_s), never",
    "stored: a record cannot decide when a later reader must stop trusting it.",
    "Delete the _what_this_is and _how_to_write keys when you copy this."
  ],
  "_how_to_write": [
    "One pool per invocation, built from an observation document the",
    "resource_observation module can read — a runtime-pack-quota-1 document from",
    "an adapter's observer, or the record `resource_observation.py --json` prints:",
    "  python3 tools/capacity_record.py write CAPACITY.json \\",
    "      --written-by 'the coordinator at a capability boundary' \\",
    "      --pool-from quota.json --pool-id pool-a \\",
    "      --kind independent --window rolling --window-name rolling_5h \\",
    "      --billing-mode subscription \\",
    "      --reserve coordinator=10,result_consumption=5,repair_and_audit=5 \\",
    "      --keep-existing",
    "--keep-existing keeps the record's other readable pools; when any existing",
    "entry cannot be parsed the write is REFUSED and the file left untouched,",
    "because a writer never silently drops a pool it could not read.",
    "Then check what stands, in a separate process, with:",
    "  python3 tools/capacity_record.py check CAPACITY.json"
  ],
